Write functions that calculates the factorial of n (i.e., n!)

Approach 1: Using For loop

Approach 2: Using Recursive algorithm\begin{align*}
n!=
\begin{cases}
  1 & \text{if $n < 1$}\\
  n*(n-1)! & \text{if $n \ge 1$}
\end{cases}    
\end{align*}

Time complexity analysis

Provide comparison of both practical (e.g. for n=600) and theoretical time complexity analysis for each approach

def factorial_for(num):
    result = 1
    for i in range(1, num + 1):
        result = result * i
    return result


def factorial_recursive(num):
    if num < 1:
        return 1
    else:
        return num * factorial_recursive(num - 1)


import time
start_time = time.time()
factorial_for(500)
time_for = time.time() - start_time
start_time = time.time()
factorial_recursive(500)
time_recursive = time.time() - start_time

print("Time for iterative approach:", round(time_for, 6), "seconds")
print("Time for recursive approach:", round(time_recursive, 6), "seconds")
